    "description": "Vijaygarh Fort is a historic hill fort located near Mau Kalan village in the Chatra block of Sonbhadra district, Uttar Pradesh, India. The fort is situated approximately 30 kilometres southeast of Robertsganj near the Dhandhraul Dam on the Chatra–Siltham road. Located within the rugged terrain of the Kaimur Range, the fort is known for its archaeological remains, rock inscriptions, perennial ponds, temples, cave paintings, and its association with the Hindi fantasy novel Chandrakanta by Devaki Nandan Khatri.",
